// Title: CrashControl CrashDump Disabled
// Sigma ID: 2ff692c2-4594-41ec-8fcb-46587de769e0
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Tobias Michalski (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-02-24 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence, stealth, defense-impairment, T1564, T1112
// Description: Detects disabling the CrashDump per registry (as used by HermeticWiper)
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate disabling of crashdumps
// References:
//   - https://www.sentinelone.com/labs/hermetic-wiper-ukraine-under-attack/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_crashdump_disabled.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\CrashControl" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)"
